SlothClash core patch 0042: warn about Snell v6 mode unsafe-raw at config load.

Snell v6 mode unsafe-raw drops the crypto as well as the profile layer: it
never uses the psk, so there is no authentication and no encryption. Traffic
to such a server is plaintext, and an unsafe-raw listener is an open proxy to
anyone who reaches its port. Citrus rejects the mode for that reason. Here it
stays accepted, as in stock mihomo, but the core logs one warning per proxy
(adapter/outbound NewSnell) and per listener (listener ParseListener) when the
config loads. default and unshaped, and Snell before v6, do not warn.

Tests: adapter/outbound and listener build unset, default, unshaped and
unsafe-raw v6 proxies and listeners (and a v4 one), capture the log through
log.Subscribe and check that each is accepted, that only unsafe-raw warns and
that it warns exactly once.

